# AIOptic

**See every token. Control every dollar.**

AIOptic is the central AI operations and cost management platform — the
"Datadog + Vercel + Stripe Dashboard" for AI infrastructure. It gives CTOs, AI
engineers, platform engineers, and finance teams complete visibility into AI
costs, usage, governance, and infrastructure across every cloud (AWS, Azure,
GCP) and every LLM provider (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Grok, Cohere, Mistral,
Together AI, OpenRouter, Ollama, and self-hosted open-source models).

## Branding

| Element    | Direction |
|------------|-----------|
| Name       | **AIOptic** — "AI" + "optic" (lens/visibility). Short, pronounceable, .dev/.ai domains have strong availability potential. |
| Tagline    | *See every token. Control every dollar.* |
| Colors     | Near-black base `#07070B`, indigo `#6366F1` → violet `#8B5CF6` gradient accents, cyan `#22D3EE` data accent, emerald `#34D399` for savings/health. |
| Typography | Geist Sans (UI/headings), Geist Mono (numbers, code, telemetry). |
| Logo style | Aperture/lens mark (currently Lucide `Aperture`) in indigo — geometric, minimal, works at 16px favicon scale. |
| Aesthetic  | Dark-mode-first, glassmorphism, aurora gradients, subtle micro-interactions — Linear/Vercel/Stripe-class polish. |

## Quick start

```bash
cd web
npm install
npm run dev      # http://localhost:3000
npm run build    # production build
npm run lint
```

Requires Node.js 18.18+.

## Tech stack

Next.js 14 (App Router) · React 18 · TypeScript · Tailwind CSS · Framer Motion
· Lucide Icons · Geist fonts. All animation respects `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Frontend architecture & folder structure

```
web/
├── src/
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── layout.tsx            # Root layout, fonts, SEO metadata (OG/Twitter)
│   │   ├── page.tsx              # Landing page (assembles all sections)
│   │   ├── globals.css           # Design tokens, glass/aurora/chart keyframes
│   │   ├── sitemap.ts            # SEO sitemap
│   │   ├── robots.ts             # SEO robots
│   │   └── dashboard/page.tsx    # Interactive SaaS dashboard demo
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── motion.tsx            # FadeIn / Stagger / Float animation primitives
│   │   ├── navbar.tsx            # Glass sticky nav + mobile menu
│   │   ├── hero.tsx              # Animated hero with floating stat cards
│   │   ├── sections.tsx          # TrustedBy, Product, Features, Integrations,
│   │   │                         #   SelfHosted, Security
│   │   ├── dashboard-preview.tsx # Landing-page live dashboard section
│   │   ├── charts.tsx            # Animated SVG charts, counters, bars
│   │   ├── pricing-faq.tsx       # Pricing, Testimonials, FAQ, Contact, Footer
│   │   └── dashboard-app.tsx     # Full dashboard shell (sidebar, table, alerts)
│   └── lib/utils.ts              # cn() class merge helper
```

Server components by default; `"use client"` only where interactivity/animation
requires it, keeping First Load JS at ~156 kB for the landing page.

## Hosting (free tiers)

1. **Vercel** (recommended) — zero-config Next.js, preview deployments, edge
   network, analytics. Connect the repo, set root directory to `web/`.
2. **Cloudflare Pages** — generous free tier, use `@cloudflare/next-on-pages`.
3. **Netlify** — solid alternative with the official Next.js runtime.

## Scalable backend architecture (future)

- **Gateway**: lightweight LLM proxy (Go/Rust) in the request path for
  real-time token/cost capture; <5ms overhead; deployable in customer VPC.
- **Ingestion**: events → Kafka/Redpanda → stream processor → ClickHouse
  (usage analytics) + Postgres (tenants, teams, budgets, RBAC).
- **Billing integrations**: scheduled pollers for AWS CUR, Azure Cost
  Management, GCP Billing export, and provider usage APIs.
- **Forecasting**: Python service (Prophet/ML) reading ClickHouse aggregates.
- **API layer**: tRPC/GraphQL over Node or Go, multi-tenant with row-level
  security; SSO via WorkOS/Auth0.
- **Self-hosted agent**: Helm-deployed collector (OpenTelemetry-based)
  streaming GPU/inference telemetry; air-gapped mode buffers locally.
- **Alerts**: rules engine → Slack/PagerDuty/email via queue workers.
